# Materialize this file and the referenced secret files on the registered
# service host through Skarbiec and keep it owner-readable.
# This dedicated config's grant may read only `brama-service/gpg_private_key`.
BRAMA_SKARBIEC_STADO_CONFIG=$HOME/.config/stado/brama-service.json
# Dedicated request-sign grant; it may read only the Content Platform, Oko,
# and Weles HMAC identity items.
BRAMA_REQUEST_SIGN_STADO_CONFIG=$HOME/.config/stado/brama-request-sign-verifier.json
# Dedicated bearer verifier grant. It may read only `token` from every explicit
# client item named by scripts/start-with-skarbiec.sh. It has no provider,
# caller, control-plane, or shared-token access.
BRAMA_MODEL_ROUTER_VERIFIER_STADO_CONFIG=$HOME/.config/stado/brama-model-router-verifier.json
# Authoritative nonsecret service policy. The launcher reads
# services.brama.{allowed_models,model_aliases,required_provider_capabilities}
# from this document and rejects absent, malformed, or inconsistent policy.
BRAMA_CONTROL_CONFIG=$HOME/.config/stado/config.json
# Owner-only route and deployment snapshot written atomically by
# `stado inference route set` on the Brama gateway target.
BRAMA_INFERENCE_ROUTES_FILE=$HOME/.stado/inference/routes.json
# The matching signed brama-runtime capability policy must authorize direct
# `provider:local-openai`, `provider:openai`, and `provider:qwen`
# authentication resources. Runtime
# capability IDs are freshly issued from those bindings; never configure IDs
# or provider credentials in this nonsecret file.
# Comma-separated TLS terminator peer IPs. Empty trusts no forwarded headers;
# direct loopback remains the only plaintext transport.
BRAMA_TRUSTED_PROXY_IPS=


# Optional provider base overrides are accepted only for that provider's exact
# built-in trusted host over HTTPS, or for an explicitly configured loopback
# URL used by a local adapter. Catalog and credential endpoint fields are not
# trusted routing configuration.
# BRAMA_PROVIDER_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com
